**Read:** MN 51–100 in [The Middle Length Discourses of the Buddha](../sources/Middle-length.lingua#r_7DP0G07DRGWNMD81GH20R1RTNB), completing this division in order. Read the general introduction with the first division and consult notes when an interpretation depends on them.

Compare teachings addressed to different interlocutors. A difference in presentation may answer a different question; it may also raise a real interpretive difficulty. Neither perfect uniformity nor contradiction should be assumed in advance.

**Work through the text:** Reconstruct two responses to an objection. Identify the argument and the practical change each seeks, and explain what a fair comparison must preserve.

**Check:** locate the passages another reader would need to challenge your reconstruction. Distinguish an example of teaching in context from a rule you have inferred for every possible audience.

**Continue:** [Majjhima III: meditation within a connected teaching](MN-Final-fifty-two.lingua#r_7C74518PAWFMJQ9KSDWB6Z3BJD).

